    "sentence_translations": [
      "Blind Imitation",
      "",
      "Xi Shi is one of the Four Great Beauties in China. Then who is Dong Shi?",
      "",
      "Dong Shi is an ugly woman.",
      "One day, Xi Shi walked down the street frowning, and everyone she met said she looked beautiful.",
      "Dong Shi noticed this, and started imitating Xi Shi by walking down the street frowning too.",
      "As a result, everyone got so frightened they ran back home, closed the doors, and did not dare come out.",
      "They said: “Dong Shi only knows that frowning looks beautiful, but she doesn't understand the real reason why.”",
      "",
      "Later people began saying “Dong Shi’s imitation” to describe imitating others blindly but ending up humiliating oneself.",
      "“Xiào” means to imitate, and “pín” means to frown.",
      "Everyone has their own strengths, so we should be ourselves instead of blindly imitating others.",
      ""
    ]
